# Behavior + A* architecture

Mob turns are a **two-library pipeline**. Do not replace either half with a custom C# brain or a home-grown path scorer.

Related design notes: [docs/behavior.md](docs/behavior.md).

## Intent (architecture goal)

| Step | Library / owner | Responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. **Decide** | **Unity Behavior** (`CreaturePolicyGraphs`, conditions, select actions) | Choose *what*: `Attack` / `Chase` / `Flee` / `Wander` / `Idle` |
| 2. **Redirect** | `CreatureHunt.Redirect` (thin glue) | Fear/hate only when personality returned Idle/Wander; sticky slime pursuit |
| 3. **Move** | **A* Pathfinding Project** via `GridPath` | Choose *where* to step this turn (grid path, Speed steps along `ab.path`) |

Personality graphs answer **policy toward the slime**. Innate fear/hate answers **mob↔mob** story fights. There is **no** `FearsSlimes` status.

## Hard rules

1. **Keep Unity Behavior for Decide.** Do not replace `CreatureBrain.Decide` with a plain-C# `switch (personality)` brain that invents intents.
2. **Keep A* Pathfinding Project for walk destinations.** `GridPath.Find` / `TryWalk` must build a temp `AstarPath` + `GridGraph`, run `ABPath`, convert **`ab.path` / `GridNodeBase` indices** (not zigzaggy `vectorPath`), then take at most `Speed` path steps.
3. **No DIY “best cell” chase.** Forbidden: ring scans around the actor, Chebyshev-greedy `BestToward` / `Filtered` pickers, custom per-turn A* written in-repo that bypasses the package.
4. **Goals are OK; move picking is not.** Listing approach cells around a target (or a flee waypoint from `PickFleeCell`) as **A\* goals** is allowed. Iterating neighbors and scoring “closest to target” as the *step* is not.
5. **Bind before tick.** Behavior conditions read `CreatureTurnContext.Actor` / bound graph `GameObject`. Proofs: `BehaviorGraphBindOwnerProofTests`.
6. **Destroy temp A\* hosts.** Always `DestroyImmediate` the temporary `AstarPath` host after the query (see `GridPath`), or later Play Mode chases silently fail.
7. **Query nodes at integer centers.** Construct paths from `GridNode` positions / aligned points — half-cell probes (`x+0.5`) snap to the wrong start and under-close Speed-2 chases.

## Allowed glue (not a third pathfinder)

- `CreatureHunt.Redirect` / `AfterAct` — fear/hate + pursuit memory after Behavior chose Idle/Wander or after an act.
- `ApproachCells` — goal set for A\* (adjacent walkable cells around the focus).
- `PickFleeCell` — single flee **waypoint** (goal). Walking to it still goes through `GridPath.TryWalk`.
- Flee may reject an A\* prefix that does not increase distance from the threat and fall back to an **adjacent** farther cell — that is still not chase-style BestToward.
- Floor penalties via `Substance.FloorPriorityFor(walker)` → node `Penalty` on the A\* graph (soft cost, not a hard block).

## Examples

### Decide: Behavior graph vs hand-rolled brain

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — custom personality brain bypasses Unity Behavior
CreatureIntent Decide(Creature self, Creature player)
{
    if (self.Personality == CreaturePersonality.Aggressive
        && CreatureMoves.CanSee(self, player))
    {
        return CreatureMoves.IsAdjacent(self, player)
            ? CreatureIntent.Attack
            : CreatureIntent.Chase;
    }

    return CreatureIntent.Idle;
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — tick the personality Behavior graph
CreatureIntent Decide(Creature self)
{
    CreatureTurnContext.SetActor(self);
    var graph = CreaturePolicyGraphs.For(self.Personality);
    CreaturePolicyGraphs.BindOwner(graph, self.gameObject);
    graph.End();
    graph.Start();
    graph.Tick();
    var intent = CreatureTurnContext.ChosenIntent;
    return intent == CreatureIntent.None ? CreatureIntent.Idle : intent;
}
```

### Chase step: A* path vs greedy neighbor score

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — DIY “best toward” (ring / neighbor heuristic). Forbidden.
Vector2Int BestToward(Vector2Int from, Vector2Int target, Func<Vector2Int, bool> blocked, int speed)
{
    Vector2Int best = from;
    var bestScore = int.MaxValue;
    for (var y = -speed; y <= speed; y++)
    for (var x = -speed; x <= speed; x++)
    {
        var cell = from + new Vector2Int(x, y);
        if (blocked(cell)) continue;
        var score = GridStep.Chebyshev(cell, target);
        if (score < bestScore) { bestScore = score; best = cell; }
    }
    return best;
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — goals only; A* Pathfinding Project picks the walk
var goals = ApproachCells(session, focus.Cell, self.Cell);
return GridPath.TryWalk(
    session.World,
    self.Cell,
    goals,
    cell => IsBlocked(session, self.Cell, cell),
    self.Speed,
    out var destination,
    self)
    && TryStep(self, session, new List<Vector2Int> { destination }, rng);
```

### Path extraction: node path vs vectorPath / Chebyshev teleport

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — walk by Chebyshev along vectorPath (teleports through blockers / zigzags)
destination = vectorPath
    .Select(ToCell)
    .Last(cell => GridStep.Chebyshev(from, cell) <= speed);
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — at most Speed indices along contiguous GridNode path
var steps = Mathf.Min(Mathf.Max(1, maxStep), path.Count);
destination = path[steps - 1];
while (steps > 0 && GridStep.Chebyshev(from, path[steps - 1]) > maxStep)
{
    steps--;
}
destination = path[steps - 1];
```

### In-repo A* that replaces the package

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — second pathfinder in World/ that “fixes” chase without the package
public static List<Vector2Int> FindDiyAstar(...) { /* PriorityQueue + neighbors */ }
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — temporary GridGraph + ABPath from A* Pathfinding Project
var gg = astar.data.AddGraph(typeof(GridGraph)) as GridGraph;
gg.neighbours = NumNeighbours.Eight;
astar.Scan(gg);
// mark Walkable / Penalty, CalculateConnections, FloodFill
var ab = ABPath.Construct((Vector3)startNode.position, (Vector3)goalNode.position, null);
AstarPath.StartPath(ab);
ab.BlockUntilCalculated();
var cells = ToCells(start, ab.path); // GridNodeBase indices, contiguous
```

### Fear/hate redirect (Idle/Wander only)

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — Combat or Decide hardcodes “dogs always chase cats”
if (self is Dog && other is Cat) return CreatureIntent.Chase;
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — Behavior returned Idle/Wander; Redirect asks statuses
if (intent != CreatureIntent.Wander && intent != CreatureIntent.Idle)
{
    return intent; // personality vs slime already decided
}

var predator = FindPredator(self, others); // StatusEffect.IsPredator
if (predator != null)
{
    CreatureTurnContext.FocusTarget = predator;
    EnsureFleeWaypoint(self, predator, session);
    return CreatureIntent.Flee;
}
```

### Hunt tests (board-only)

Mob↔mob hunts must **not** require a slime. Prefer `SessionFactory.Board` + `TakeTurn(..., player: null)`. Do not inflate the map or park a slime at `(19,19)` to dodge Aggressive vision — see [docs/architecture/dependency-inversion.md](docs/architecture/dependency-inversion.md).

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — fake far slime so Aggressive never steals focus
var player = Spawn<Slime>(new Vector2Int(19, 19));
dog.TakeTurn(session, player, rng, others);
```

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — no controlled player; hunt redirect owns intents
var session = SessionFactory.Board(world, dog, cat);
dog.TakeTurn(session, player: null, rng, others);
```

## Checklist before merging AI / path changes

- [ ] Decide still ticks Unity Behavior (`CreaturePolicyGraphs` / conditions).
- [ ] Walk still goes through `GridPath` → A* Pathfinding Project.
- [ ] No new neighbor-ring / BestToward / Filtered chase picker.
- [ ] Temp `AstarPath` host destroyed; paths contiguous from the real start node.
- [ ] Focused EditMode: `BehaviorRulesTests`, `GridPathTests`, `DogCatHuntSimulationTests` as relevant.
